data: {"type":"response.reasoning.done","sequence_number":374,"item_id":"rs_1793301520393_640qwymldzb","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"Here's a thinking process:\n\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\n   - Question: \"Is 91 a prime number?\"\n   - Format requirements: Answer \"yes\" or \"no\" with one short reason.\n\n2.  **Determine Mathematical Fact:**\n   - Need to check if 91 is prime.\n   - A prime number has exactly two distinct positive divisors: 1 and itself.\n   - Check divisibility: 91 is not even, not divisible by 3 (9+1=10, not divisible by 3).\n   - Check divisibility by 7: 7 * 13 = 91. Yes!\n   - So 91 = 7 × 13, meaning it has divisors other than 1 and itself.\n   - Conclusion: 91 is not a prime number; it's composite.\n\n3.  **Format Output:**\n   - Must answer \"yes\" or \"no\".\n   - Must include one short reason.\n   - Format: \"no\" + short reason.\n   - Example: \"no, because 91 = 7 × 13.\"\n\n   Wait, the prompt says: \"Answer yes or no with one short reason.\" It might mean the whole answer should be just the word and the reason, possibly concise. I'll output: \"no, because 91 = 7 × 13.\" Or maybe just \"no, it's divisible by 7 and 13.\" I'll keep it short.\n\n   Let's verify: 91 / 7 = 13. Yes.\n   So answer: no.\n\n   I'll output: \"no, because 91 = 7 × 13.\" That fits \"yes or no with one short reason.\"\n\n   Check constraints: \n   - Yes/No answer: \"no\"\n   - One short reason: \"because 91 = 7 × 13\"\n   All good.\n\n   Final output formatting: just the text. I'll make sure it's exactly as requested.✅"}

